/tools/emu/target/
# `rsk-emu --store <path>` writes a flash image, and that image holds the device
# seed in the clear — there is no OTP root under an emulator to seal it to. The
# default path is the working directory, so this is the difference between a
# throwaway test key and one committed to a public repository.
*.store

# TLC output: one log per configuration (`formal/run-tlc.sh`), plus the state
# directory TLC creates for its fingerprint set. NOTHING here is committed. A
# summary table used to be, "so the README's results table stays auditable" --
# but no script wrote it, so it was a hand-saved snapshot that went stale the
# week after. What makes the table auditable is `deep-checks.yml`'s weekly
# `formal` row: it runs the whole tier and publishes the matrix to the step
# summary, and `floors.txt` fails the run when a row stops producing its own.
/formal/out/*
/formal/states/

# Documentation site: build output and the mermaid assets that
# `mdbook-mermaid install` generates next to book.toml (not committed).
/book/
/site/
/mermaid.min.js
/mermaid-init.js
